text.section:
The Commission may revoke a certificate of authority of a foreign savings institution if:

The institution fails to conduct its business in the Commonwealth in a manner consistent with the laws of the Commonwealth;


The affairs of the institution are in an unsafe condition;


The institution refuses to comply with the orders of the Commission or refuses to comply with a request by the Commissioner to review the books and records of the institution; or


The institution fails to pay any fees or taxes imposed by the laws of the Commonwealth.
